2. Third-party components that the build downloads
--------------------------------------------------
This repository does not contain these components. The scripts, and Gradle,
download them from their upstream repositories onto the machine that builds
Conduit.

The ViaVersion artifacts below are NOT in a Conduit distribution. They are GPL
object code, and Conduit does not convey them: a running proxy downloads them
from repo.viaversion.com into lib/via on the operator's own machine. They are
listed here because Conduit links against them and runs in one process with
them. Anyone who passes on a populated lib/via alongside the jar is conveying
Via as well, and needs Via's Corresponding Source from the matching upstream
tags; scripts/fetch-via-source.ps1 fetches those archives.

Everything else below is in the jar, which carries this file, LICENSE (with the
GPLv3 text) and, under source/, the Corresponding Source for Conduit. See
docs/LICENSING_VIA.md.

